==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈpɒti/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-potty.wav|a=Southern England}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɒti|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{suffix|en|pot|y|t1=chamberpot|pos2=diminutive suffix}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A [[chamber pot]].
# A small, usually plastic, chamber pot used to [[toilet-train]] small [[children]].
#* {{quote-book|en|title=''In the Money''|author=w:William Carlos Williams|year=1940|passage=If you just let him know you want him to go on the '''potty''', or anything, he's miles away.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Your Child Makes Sense: A Guidebook for Parents|author=Edith Buxbaum|year=1949|passage=Mothers very often make the baby and themselves unhappy by setting the child on the '''potty''' every hour.}}
# {{lb|en|childish|humorous}} [[any|Any]] [[other]] [[device]] or [[place]] for [[urination]] or [[defecation]]: a [[toilet]]; a [[lavatory]]; a [[latrine]]; an [[outhouse]].

